{"awe":{"w":"awe","zh":["敬畏"],"ipa":{"uk":"/ɔː/","us":"/ɔː/"},"ety":[{"n":1,"chain":[{"l":"enm","f":"aw","t":"inh"},{"l":"non","f":"agi","t":"der"},{"l":"gem-pro","f":"*agaz","t":"der","g":"terror, dread"},{"l":"ine-pro","f":"*h₂egʰ-","t":"der","g":"to be upset, afraid"}],"text":"From Middle English aw, awe, agh, awȝe, borrowed from Old Norse agi, from Proto-Germanic *agaz (“terror, dread”), from Proto-Indo-European *h₂egʰ- (“to be upset, afraid”). Displaced native Middle English eye, eyȝe, ayȝe, eȝȝe, from Old English ege, æge (“fear, terror, dread”), from the same Proto-Germanic root.","cog":[{"l":"enm","f":"eye"},{"l":"ang","f":"ege"}]},{"n":2,"chain":[{"l":"fr","f":"auve","t":"bor"}],"text":"Borrowed from French auve."}],"pos":[{"p":"noun","e":0,"senses":[{"d":"A feeling of fear and reverence.","tags":["uncountable"],"grp":0,"zh":"敬畏"},{"d":"A feeling of amazement.","tags":["uncountable"],"grp":1},{"d":"Power to inspire awe.","tags":["archaic","uncountable"]}],"forms":[["pl","awes"]]},{"p":"verb","e":0,"senses":[{"d":"To inspire fear and reverence in.","tags":["transitive"],"syn":["enthral","enthrall","overwhelm"],"grp":2},{"d":"To control by inspiring dread.","tags":["transitive"]}],"forms":[["3s","awes"],["ing","awing"],["ing","aweing"],["pp","awed"],["past","awed"]]},{"p":"noun","e":1,"senses":[{"d":"A bucket (blade) attached to water wheels.","tags":["obsolete"]}],"forms":[["pl","awes"]]}],"grp":[{"label":"feeling of fear and reverence","zh":["敬畏"],"p":"noun","e":0,"tr":{"fr":["fr:crainte","fr:révérence"],"it":["it:timore"],"es":["es:pavor","es:temor","es:medrosía"],"pt":["pt:temor"]}},{"label":"feeling of amazement","zh":[],"p":"noun","e":0,"tr":{"fr":["fr:admiration"],"it":[],"es":["es:asombro"],"pt":["pt:espanto","pt:admiração"]}},{"label":"to inspire fear and reverence","zh":[],"p":"verb","e":0,"tr":{"fr":[],"it":[],"es":["es:asombrar","es:abrumar","es:zozobrar"],"pt":[]}}],"lx":{"fr:crainte":{"w":"crainte","p":"noun","g":"f","art":"la","pl":"craintes","plArt":"les","ipa":"/kʁɛ̃t/","gl":"fear, fright","ety":{"chain":[],"text":"From craindre + -te. Attested since the 13th century; replaced Old French crieme.","form":{"l":"fr","parts":["craindre","-te"]}}},"fr:révérence":{"w":"révérence","p":"noun","g":"f","art":"la","pl":"révérences","plArt":"les","ipa":"/ʁe.ve.ʁɑ̃s/","gl":"reverence (deep respect)","ety":{"chain":[{"l":"la","f":"reverentia","t":"der","g":"timidity, shyness (due to respect)"}],"text":"From Latin reverentia."}},"it:timore":{"w":"timore","p":"noun","g":"m","art":"il","pl":"timori","plArt":"i","ipa":"/tiˈmo.re/","gl":"fear, dread, worry, alarm","ety":{"chain":[{"l":"la","f":"timōrem","t":"der","lm":"timor","g":"fear, dread"}],"text":"From Latin timōrem. Cf. also Old Italian temore, which was likely altered to reflect the Latin more closely."}},"es:pavor":{"w":"pavor","p":"noun","g":"m","art":"el","pl":"pavores","plArt":"los","ipa":"/paˈboɾ/","gl":"dread, fright, fear","ety":{"chain":[{"l":"la","f":"pavōrem","t":"der","lm":"pavor","g":"The act of trembling, quaking, throbbing or panting with fear."}],"text":"From Latin pavōrem. It may be a semi-learned term in its current form, preserving the intervocalic 'v' unlike other non-Iberian Romance cognates (compare the attested Old Spanish form paor); descendants of Latin metus (e.g. Spanish miedo) were the primary words for \"fear\" on the Iberian peninsula."}},"es:temor":{"w":"temor","p":"noun","g":"m","art":"el","pl":"temores","plArt":"los","ipa":"/teˈmoɾ/","gl":"fear; dread","ety":{"chain":[{"l":"la","f":"timōrem","t":"inh","lm":"timor","g":"fear, dread"}],"text":"Inherited from Latin timōrem, whence English timorous."}},"es:medrosía":{"w":"medrosía","g":"f","art":"la"},"pt:temor":{"w":"temor","p":"noun","g":"m","art":"o","pl":"temores","plArt":"os","ipaBR":"/teˈmoʁ/","ipa":"/teˈmoʁ/","ipaPT":"/tɨˈmoɾ/","gl":"fear (emotion caused by actual or perceived danger or threat)","ety":{"chain":[{"l":"roa-opt","f":"temor","t":"inh"},{"l":"la","f":"timōrem","t":"in